<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Azad Hind</h1><p class="st-meta">1943 CE – 1945 CE · capital Singapore</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A provisional government of free India led by Subhas Chandra Bose and backed by Japan during the Second World War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose">Subhas Chandra Bose</a>, a former president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>, escaped <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a> in 1941 and reached Japanese-held <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/singapore">Singapore</a> in 1943. There he took command of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-army">Indian National Army</a>, made up largely of Indian prisoners of war, and in October 1943 proclaimed the Provisional Government of Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government was recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and their allies and declared war on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>. Japan handed it nominal authority over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andaman-and-nicobar-islands">Andaman and Nicobar Islands</a>, but real control stayed with the Japanese navy. It ran its own currency, courts and a women's unit, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rani-of-jhansi-regiment">Rani of Jhansi Regiment</a>, and recruited among Indians in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-army">Indian National Army</a> joined the failed Japanese offensive on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-imphal">Imphal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kohima">Kohima</a> in 1944. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> surrender in 1945 the government collapsed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose">Bose</a> died after a plane crash in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Taiwan</a>. The trials of its officers at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-fort">Red Fort</a> stirred nationalist feeling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/azad-hind.jpg" alt="Azad Hind" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Nicholas (Nichalp) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1931_Flag_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1943 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Singapore</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Subhas Chandra Bose</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hindustani, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provisional Government of Free India, Arzi Hukumat-e-Azad Hind</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=azad-hind" aria-label="Azad Hind on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7231 1743 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Azad Hind lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7551 1999L8529 1145"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8529 1145h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7551 1999h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7551 1999h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=azad-hind">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

